n or discard predecessor checkpoints. Use /Users/iv/.curator/global/bin/task-board exclusively. Confirm worktree refresh-candidate --help describes initial as well as rework candidates; if absent, report exact installation mismatch instead of looping handoff.\\n\\nWith your live tracked producer ownership and exclusive Story lease, run task-board worktree refresh-candidate TASK-260830-21gygk. The candidate must already combine current trunk and remain unstaged. The fixed command accepts a provably absent first CR, preserves candidate files, replays checkpoints with signing and reconciles managed metadata. Never fabricate CRs, hand-commit Story checkpoints, edit registries or reset/clean the worktree. Inspect any refusal and preserve its exact evidence.\\n\\nAfter successful refresh verify the current checkpoint descends from selected fresh authority and candidate content is intact. Run the relevant configured local validation against the resulting candidate, attach exact logs and outcome and hand off normally to publish the real initial CR. Hosted CI stays disabled. The orchestrator will spawn an independent Astra medium reviewer; this producer must not accept, integrate or land the Story.\\n\\nInclude durable evidence for previous mutation claims or state their actual limitations. All assigned shared API semantics remain required, including the full 14.7.2 plan/fact binding and 14.7.3 summaries; existing outcome claims do not reduce scope. Apply only necessary corrective work, with truthful attribution to earlier evidence and fresh validation where candidate changes require it.\\n===BOUND-REPLAY===\\nResume TASK-260830-21gygk only after the orchestrator verifies the BUG-260910-1nfu12 task-board fix is landed and installed. Use /Users/iv/.curator/global/bin/task-board. Existing product candidate and predecessor checkpoints must be preserved; no independent Story landing or manual checkpoint commits.\\n\\nThe previous fe37d7 run reached the signed isolated replay and found exactly one additive LOGBOOK.md conflict; production code applied cleanly. Read TASK-260830-21gygk_refresh-refusal-fe37d7.md and the durable TASK-260830-21gygk_evidence-fe37d7.tar.gz/results evidence. Existing source validation is reusable if its candidate hashes match; do not redo implementation or repeat a mutation battery solely because a new run began. Actual CR validation and subsequent independent review remain mandatory.\\n\\nConfirm refresh-candidate --help exposes --replay-resolutions. Run the ordinary refresh once to obtain a new retained conflict worktree and its adjacent resolution-template.json. This first conflict is expected and is not a handoff or a product blocker. Inspect the actual unmerged paths and REBASE_HEAD in the retained worktree. For the measured LOGBOOK conflict, preserve both additive blocks in chronological newest-first order. Resolve the earlier checkpoint's log content, not an entire newer final-leaf LOGBOOK that would absorb uncommitted leaf documentation. Do not edit or commit the retained replay; prepare the chosen replacement bytes in task-scoped scratch storage.\\n\\nCopy resolution-template.json to a task-scoped packet outside the candidate (under .temp). Keep its version/branch_oid/trunk_oid/candidate_tree_oid unchanged. Add resolutions entries with checkpoint_oid equal to the actual original REBASE_HEAD, path equal to the exact unmerged relative path, content as base64 bytes of the chosen replacement, and sha256 as lowercase hex SHA-256 of those decoded bytes. Python json/base64/hashlib can prepare the packet. The installed command verifies every binding, applies only actual conflict paths and signs replay continuation.\\n\\nRun task-board worktree refresh-candidate TASK-260830-21gygk --replay-resolutions FILE with your live producer lease. It reconstructs replay from original checkpoints, preserves live candidate bytes and durably updates branch/index/metadata. Never fabricate CRs or registry state, hand-commit checkpoints, reset/clean the worktree or configure an AX-specific merge driver. If additional conflicts arise, inspect and explicitly resolve their exact checkpoint/path scope; regenerate only from the current authoritative template and evidence. Surface an objective unsatisfied gate with exact evidence, never repeatedly handoff into a known unchanged refusal.\\n\\nAfter success verify the checkpoint descends from fresh main and the complete candidate bytes are intact. Attach resolution packet and exact command/evidence as task-scoped outcomes, then use normal producer handoff to publish the real CR. Public shared-library scope remains v0.6.0 14.7/14.7.1/14.7.2 and summaries5.7/14.7.3; previous 8/8 claims are not independent acceptance. The orchestrator owns Astra medium review, rework routing and final Story delivery.\\n===BOARD-RESOURCES===\\nmutation error: parse error at 1:1: unknown operation \\\"list_resources\\\" (got \\\"list_resources\\\"); known operations: accept_cr, add_checklist_item, add_resource, assign, audit_context_validation, check_item, collect_context_retention, confirm_context_reclamation, correct_activity, create, delete, delete_resource, handoff, link, login, logout, mark_context_stale, normalize_legacy_status, publish_context, reclassify_context, record_ledger_event, register_context, remove_checklist_item, rename, retire_context, retry_context_payload_withdrawal, set_details, set_estimate, set_notes, set_parent, set_status, sweep_context_retention, sweep_context_validation_audits, switch_user, unassign, uncheck_item, unlink, update_resource, withdraw_cr; see schema() for the contract and schema(mutation=NAME) for one signature\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 6291,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 1573,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","final_result":true}}}
